{%- comment -%}
  RETIRED 30 AUGUST 2026. Operator decision.

  This snippet used to put the joining gift in the cart drawer: an offer
  line and a button that opened the newsletter popup. It is removed, not
  because it failed, but because a discount prompt at the moment of
  purchase sends people out of the bag to hunt for a code. The operator
  did exactly that himself while testing on 30 August. Neither reference
  brand carries any capture inside the cart.

  NOTHING IS LOST BY REMOVING IT. The newsletter popup captures on every
  page and is the only capture on this site proven to work. And since
  30 August the discount attaches itself by cookie through
  /discount/WELCOME, so the bag never needs to mention a code.

  THE DRAWER SPACE RULES BELOW ARE STILL LIVE and are the only reason
  this file still renders anything. They stop the footer crushing the
  product list on a phone. If they are ever moved into a stylesheet,
  this file can be deleted and its render line removed from
  snippets/cart-drawer.liquid.

  DO NOT REBUILD A CAPTURE HERE. Shopify refuses POST /contact from
  anything that is not a real browser form navigation: 400 from fetch in
  the browser, 403 from curl using the popup's own exact payload. The
  drawer is also inside CartDrawerForm, so a nested <form> is dropped by
  the parser. Five versions proved this on 30 August.
{%- endcomment -%}

<style>
  /* Drawer space, 30 Aug 2026. The footer had grown so tall that the
     product list collapsed to a single row on a phone. Presentation
     only. No wording is touched, including the age and terms label,
     which is with the solicitor. */
  #CartDrawer .drawer__scrollable{min-height:38vh}
  #CartDrawer .cart__terms label{letter-spacing:0;text-transform:none;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35}
  #CartDrawer .cart__item-row{padding-top:6px;padding-bottom:6px}
  #CartDrawer .cart__checkout-wrapper{margin-top:8px}
</style>
